S1       THE GROUP ACTION ON CS, COMPUTED
         CS lives in R/(1/2)Z.  The three bits act as (all three ESTABLISHED, not
         assumed -- xB015 K6 494/494, xB018 C5 240/240, xB020 H2 derived):
           A5 : x -> x + 1/4     A7 : x -> -x     A6 : x -> -x  (conjugation)
         |<A5, A7=A6>| = 4
         STABILISER of the object's value CS = 0: order 2 -> [(-1, Fraction(0, 1)), (1, Fraction(0, 1))]
           = {identity, negation} = {A6, A7}
         ORBIT of 0: [Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(1, 4)]   (orbit-stabiliser: 4 = 2 x 2)
         on the 2-torsion {0, 1/4}: A7 and A6 act TRIVIALLY; A5 SWAPS the two.
S1 PASS  A6 AND A7 ARE EXACTLY THE STABILISER OF THE OBJECT.
         A5 IS THE ORBIT DIRECTION.  Not an analogy -- a computed orbit-stabiliser.

